  "usage_note": "**Such** goes before the article **a** or **an**, not after it: *such a good idea*, never *a such good idea*. With a plural or uncountable noun, no article follows: *such people*, *such advice*. Learners sometimes confuse **such** with **so**, which goes directly before an adjective or adverb without a noun (*so good*, not *such good*).",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "It was a such good movie.",
      "correct": "It was such a good movie.",
      "note": "**Such** comes before the article **a**, not after it."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "The weather was such bad.",
      "correct": "The weather was so bad.",
      "note": "Directly before an adjective with no noun, **so** is used, not **such**."
